exits 0 coroner timeline export --help
cmp stdout coroner_timeline_export.txt
! stderr .

exits 0 coroner timeline list --help
cmp stdout coroner_timeline_list.txt
! stderr .

exits 0 coroner timeline use --help
cmp stdout coroner_timeline_use.txt
! stderr .

exits 0 coroner timeline view --help
cmp stdout coroner_timeline_view.txt
! stderr .

exits 0 coroner version --help
cmp stdout coroner_version.txt
! stderr .

# help <topic> exits 0 and prints the topic on stdout.
exits 0 coroner help exit-codes
stdout .
! stderr .

# An unknown topic exits 2, kind usage, with the envelope as the last line of stderr.
exits 2 coroner help tiem --json
! stdout .
stderr '^\{"error":\{"kind":"usage","message":"[^\n]+","hint":"[^\n]+"\}\}\n\z'

-- coroner.txt --
coroner records what happened during an investigation, in order: name a timeline,
add timestamped events from logs, chat and people, then view and export it.

USAGE
  coroner <command> [flags]

CORE COMMANDS
  annotation   Attach evidence and comments to events and timelines
  attachment   List, delete and export files attached to events and annotations
  event        Add, list, view, edit, delete and link events
  import       Import records from a JSONL export
  overlay      Save sets of timelines to read together
  source       List sources and fix their names
  tag          List the tags events carry
  timeline     Create, list and switch between timelines

ADDITIONAL COMMANDS
  agent        Print what coding agents need to drive coroner
  completion   Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help         Help about any command or topic
  status       Show the database and the timeline commands act on
  version      Show coroner's version

HELP TOPICS
  environment  Environment variables coroner reads
  exit-codes   Exit codes and the JSON error envelope
  formatting   Output formats and what scripts can rely on
  time         How coroner reads the times you type
  reference    Every command and flag on one Markdown page

EXAMPLES
  $ coroner timeline create checkout-outage --title "Checkout outage"
  $ coroner event add -t checkout-outage "Error rate crossed 5%" --at 2026-09-11T03:14Z --source datadog
  $ coroner event list -t checkout-outage

FLAGS
      --version   Show coroner's version

GLOBAL FLAGS
      --config path     Config file path (env: CORONER_CONFIG)
      --db path         Database file path (env: CORONER_DB)
      --debug           Print debug detail on stderr (env: CORONER_DEBUG)
      --format format   Output format: {text | json | jsonl}, and more on timeline export (default "text")
  -h, --help            Show help for a command
      --json            Short for --format json
      --no-color        Disable color (env: NO_COLOR, CORONER_NO_COLOR)
      --no-input        Never open a form, picker or viewer (env: CORONER_NO_INPUT)
  -q, --quiet           Print only essential output
      --tz zone         Time zone for this invocation (default: config default_timezone, then TZ)

LEARN MORE
  Use `coroner <command> --help` for more information about a command.
  Report bugs and send feedback at https://github.com/macintacos/coroner/issues
-- coroner_agent.txt --
coroner ships an Agent Skill that teaches coding agents to build timelines with flags and
JSON. 'coroner agent skill' prints the one this binary was built with.

USAGE
  coroner agent [flags]
  coroner agent <command> [flags]

COMMANDS
  skill        Print the Agent Skill for this version of coroner

EXAMPLES
